        "original_id": "d44757fc-860e-5903-a2fa-c7fdbf7e67c2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Baidu Baike, Chinese Wikipedia\n- Organizations: Wikimedia Foundation\n- Concepts: Baidu 10 Mythical Creatures, Internet memes\n- Places: People's Republic of China\n\nFacts:\n- Baidu Baike released its test version on 20 April 2006.\n- Within three weeks of its test release, Baidu Baike grew to more than 90,000 articles and surpassed Chinese Wikipedia in article count.\n- Chinese Wikipedia is the Standard Chinese-language edition of Wikipedia.\n- Chinese Wikipedia is run by the Wikimedia Foundation.\n- The Baidu 10 Mythical Creatures, also called the Ten Baidu Deities, originated as a humorous hoax from Baidu Baike.\n- In early 2009, the Baidu 10 Mythical Creatures became a popular and widespread Internet meme in the People's Republic of China.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "101f8fdf-8112-5562-b504-0656a8ce33a9",
        "text": "Page: Baidu Baike. Sentence: Its test version was released on 20 April 2006, and within three weeks the encyclopedia had grown to more than 90,000 articles surpassing the number in Chinese Wikipedia.\nPage: Chinese Wikipedia. Sentence: The Chinese Wikipedia () is the (Standard) Chinese language edition of Wikipedia.\nPage: Chinese Wikipedia. Sentence: It is run by the Wikimedia Foundation.\nPage: Baidu 10 Mythical Creatures. Sentence: The Baidu 10 Mythical Creatures (), alternatively Ten Baidu Deities, was initially a humorous hoax from the interactive encyclopedia Baidu Baike which became a popular and widespread Internet meme in the People's Republic of China in early 2009.",
